{"agent":"impact","findings":[{"id":"impact-1","file":"triggarr/web/routes.py","line":45,"title":"Revert of commit e11187e brings back the deprecated Jinja2Templates **env_options path, and the unpinned Docker install can crash the app when it starts","category":"breaking-api","cwe":null,"severity":"high","agent_confidence":58,"in_diff":true,"intent_doc_match":null,"problem":"This diff undoes HEAD commit e11187e ('fix: use preconfigured jinja2.Environment for autoescape'). That commit's message says newer Starlette dropped the **env_options passthrough on Jinja2Templates. In the locked Starlette 0.52.1 (.venv starlette/templating.py:92-96), the passthrough still works but always raises a DeprecationWarning: 'Extra environment options are deprecated. Use a preconfigured jinja2.Environment instead.' I confirmed this by running `python -W error::DeprecationWarning -c 'import triggarr.web.routes'`, which fails. The Dockerfile (line 31) runs `pip install .` with an unpinned `fastapi` dependency (pyproject.toml:15). It does not install from uv.lock, so image builds pick up the newest Starlette. When a Starlette release removes **env_options, as the deprecation announces and the reverted commit says has already happened, `Jinja2Templates(directory=..., autoescape=True)` raises TypeError while the module is being imported. routes.py is imported by triggarr/__main__.py and triggarr/search/scheduler.py, so the whole daemon fails to start, not only the web UI. pending: confirm which Starlette version removes **env_options. On the locked 0.52.1 the only effect today is the warning.","current_code":"templates = Jinja2Templates(directory=str(TEMPLATES_DIR), autoescape=True)","fix_hint":"Keep the preconfigured jinja2.Environment(loader=FileSystemLoader(...), autoescape=True) passed as env=, i.e. drop this revert; optionally pin starlette/fastapi upper bound or install from uv.lock in Docker.","why_it_matters":"If this breaks, the app crashes at import time on a fresh Docker build, which is a complete outage for every deployment that pulls the new image. Autoescape is the project's XSS control for templates, and it would now depend on a deprecated, version-dependent API.","silenced_marker_nearby":false},{"id":"impact-2","file":"triggarr/web/routes.py","line":45,"title":"Autoescape now depends on Starlette's deprecated passthrough and default instead of an explicit Environment","category":"blast-radius","cwe":"CWE-79","severity":"low","agent_confidence":35,"in_diff":true,"intent_doc_match":null,"problem":"On the locked Starlette 0.52.1, _create_env (templating.py:112-116) uses setdefault('autoescape', True), so autoescape stays on. The control is not weakened today. It now depends on a deprecated keyword passthrough, where before it was set explicitly on a jinja2.Environment the project owned. pending: a Starlette version that accepts directory= but drops or ignores the autoescape kwarg, or changes the default, would demonstrate a real loss of escaping.","current_code":"templates = Jinja2Templates(directory=str(TEMPLATES_DIR), autoescape=True)","fix_hint":"Restore the explicit jinja2.Environment(autoescape=True) passed via env=.","why_it_matters":"Every HTML template rendered by routes.py relies on autoescape to block XSS, including values that come back from the Radarr/Sonarr APIs.","silenced_marker_nearby":false}],"agent_notes":["The diff is a direct revert of HEAD commit e11187e, which switched to env=jinja2.Environment(...) because, per its message, Starlette removed the **env_options passthrough. Nothing in this diff explains why that fix is being undone.","Locked environment: starlette 0.52.1 still accepts **env_options but warns every time (templating.py:92-96). Running with -W error::DeprecationWarning makes the import of triggarr.web.routes fail. pytest has no filterwarnings=error, so the test suite will probably still pass and will not catch this.","Docker deployment risk: the Dockerfile runs `pip install .` (line 31) with fastapi unpinned in pyproject.toml, so uv.lock is ignored and the newest Starlette gets installed. Once a Starlette version without the passthrough is installed, the error happens at import time.","Blast radius: routes.py is imported by triggarr/__main__.py and triggarr/search/scheduler.py, and by tests/test_web.py and tests/test_middleware.py. If the import fails, the whole daemon fails, including the scheduler, not just the UI.","No schema, migration or performance impact: the template environment is built once when the module loads.","Verdict: this is not shippable as a revert. Keep the preconfigured jinja2.Environment from e11187e, unless there is a specific reason for the revert that this diff does not show."]}
